 "productionNotes": "Lotus publishes no US production figure for the Series 2 Elise, and the NHTSA exemption filings give only a company ceiling: Lotus told the agency it had never built more than 6,000 vehicles in any year. The working numbers come from owners. A LotusTalk compilation built from registries and Certificates of Vehicle Provenance issued by the Lotus archivist estimates 6,325 US Elises and Exiges for model years 2005 through 2011; Hagerty says over 6,000, about half of them 2005 Elises. Year by year the compilation gives 3,321 cars for 2005 (all Elise), 1,417 for 2006 (1,079 Elise, 338 Exige, with a note that some believe 271 Exiges), 735 for 2007, 425 for 2008, 146 for 2009, 95 for 2010 and 186 for 2011. A second compilation from 2017 says the archivist's own 2005 figure moved from 3,321 to 3,324 to 3,323 as certificates were reissued, and that the archives are not very detailed. The two compilations also disagree on the 2006 Elise (1,079 or 1,080), the 2008 Elise (77 or 78), the 2008 California Edition (46 or 50) and the 2009 Elise SC (46 or 47). For 2011 Hagerty cites LotusTalk for 128 US cars, a figure that matches neither the 186 total nor the 114 Elise R and Elise SC cars in the compilation. productionTotal is left null for that reason. These are counts of certificated and registered cars, not factory records. US list prices: $39,985 base for 2005 per MotorWeek, $41,725 including $795 destination per Forbes, and $54,990 for the 2008 Elise SC per AutoGuide, the last single-sourced. No documented US list price for the 2011 Elise R or the special editions was found.",
